<http://data.silknow.org/object/3342a7cf-bc96-38c4-8112-1117319c3a57/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The earliest samplers were reference works for embroiderers. They showed 'samples' of patterns and stitches and recorded how to achieve particular effects.  In Europe in the 17th century samplers provided instruction and practice for girls learning needlework. This example continues the tradition of stitch and pattern exercises. It is very skilfully made and may be the work of an older, more experienced needleworker. The central picture is a scene from the New Testament story of Christ and the Woman of Samaria."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/3342a7cf-bc96-38c4-8112-1117319c3a57> .

